 "checkout-api", "summary": "After the latest deploy (v2.3.1), checkout-api failed health checks in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of about 18%. The previous release candidate, v2.3.1-rc, was also unhealthy. We rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release, in all production regions. After the rollback the service reports healthy and the error rate is about 0.2%. Next steps: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 regression before redeploying it.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "confidence": 0.92}, "confidence": 0.92}, {"t_ms": 53308, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01Yc1mLWnQbyvxAedw5CD1SR", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["reconcile_lookup", "reconciled_executed", "postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 53308, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01Yc1mLWnQbyvxAedw5CD1SR", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 60165, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged on-call.\n\n- **Before:** v2.3.1 was running in us-east, us-west and eu-west. It was failing health checks with about an 18% error rate.\n- **Version chosen:** v2.3.0 is the most recent healthy release. The deployment list isn't in order, so I went by release sequence. The two releases after v2.3.0 (v2.3.1-rc and v2.3.1) were both unhealthy.\n- **After:** all three regions are on v2.3.0, health checks pass, and the error rate is about 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 describes the failure, the rollback and the recovery. It says the cause of the v2.3.1 problem should be found before that version is deployed again. There were no other open incidents, so it isn't a duplicate.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_014S2FpcsbT1oCWhWhFeVa21", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01UeuE1rD62m44jdKt3EuDtM", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The most recent healthy release by sequence is v2.3.0. v2.3.1-rc (seq 2) and v2.3.1 (seq 3) are both unhealthy.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_011gLMBpGGb1hoaHV252hgy7", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0", "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01J13UsoQyatcoNEhCCsktBM", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01DW8xm8xtCcjaBXnHCBq5tx", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"confidence": 0.9}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Yc1mLWnQbyvxAedw5CD1SR", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After the latest deploy (v2.3.1), checkout-api failed health checks in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of about 18%. The previous release candidate, v2.3.1-rc, was also unhealthy. We rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release, in all production regions. After the rollback the service reports healthy and the error rate is about 0.2%. Next steps: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 regression before redeploying it.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "confidence": 0.92}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged on-call.\n\n- **Before:** v2.3.1 was running in us-east, us-west and eu-west. It was failing health checks with about an 18% error rate.\n- **Version chosen:** v2.3.0 is the most recent healthy release. The deployment list isn't in order, so I went by release sequence. The two releases after v2.3.0 (v2.3.1-rc and v2.3.1) were both unhealthy.\n- **After:** all three regions are on v2.3.0, health checks pass, and the error rate is about 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 describes the failure, the rollback and the recovery. It says the cause of the v2.3.1 problem should be found before that version is deployed again. There were no other open incidents, so it isn't a duplicate.", "type": "text"}]}]}